.etymd/cache/
# Local-only map from a legacy corpus manifest entry's name to its directory.
sources.local.json
# Fleet sweep delta baselines are local-only (the README tells manifest repos the same).
*.fleet.json
# Machine-local notes. Operating detail — release mechanics above all — attracts account and
# environment specifics, which a public repo must never carry. The pattern is the guard: the
# runbook has a home that is not a tracked file, so the detail stops reaching for one.
*.local.md

# Machine-local companion hooks and scratch; never tracked. Root-anchored so a nested `local/`
# stays trackable. Expendable by design: `git clean -fdx` and a fresh clone both drop it —
# keep anything precious outside the tree.
/local/
